From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000029 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@local>
Date: Mon, 11 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mips: sf2000: keep timer IRQ unmasked

The physical log reaches before-calibrate-delay after the first IRQ enable.
The previous physical-only mask clearing left Status.IM at zero, preventing
the CP0 timer interrupt from advancing jiffies during calibrate_delay().

Keep IP7 unmasked while continuing to mask the other CP0 interrupt sources.
---
 init/main.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/init/main.c
+++ b/init/main.c
@@ -137,9 +137,9 @@ static void sf2000_before_irq_enable(void)
 	sf2000_progress_mark("irq-compare-before", 4, read_c0_compare());
 	if (sf2000_rom_handoff_present() &&
 	    ((read_c0_ebase() & 0xfffff000u) == 0x81002000u)) {
-		clear_c0_status(ST0_IM);
+		change_c0_status(ST0_IM, STATUSF_IP7);
 		irq_disable_hazard();
-		sf2000_progress_mark("irq-mask-cleared", 4,
+		sf2000_progress_mark("irq-mask-timer-only", 4,
 			read_c0_status());
 	}
 }
-- 
